      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(scripts): keep format-docs output tails UTF-8 safe",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where `scripts/format-docs.mjs` could render a replacement\ncharacter (&#xfffd;) in failure diagnostics when a formatter (oxfmt) error\noutput exceeded the 16 KiB tail cap and the byte window started inside a\nmultibyte UTF-8 character.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`outputTail` took a byte-bounded suffix with\n`bytes.subarray(-N).toString(\"utf8\")` before decoding.  When the retained\nbyte window started at a UTF-8 continuation byte the tail began with a\nreplacement character.  A new `decodeUtf8Tail` helper now skips any\nleading continuation bytes, matching the existing pattern from the sibling\nfix in `scripts/run-additional-boundary-checks.mjs` (#109167).\n\n## User Impact\n\nDocs formatting failure diagnostics stay readable when capped output\ncontains multibyte text (e.g. oxfmt errors on CJK documentation pages) at\nthe retention boundary.  No behaviour change for ASCII-only output.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Before the fix, `node -e` confirmed that the last 4 bytes of\n  `Buffer.from(\"你好\")` (boundary at continuation byte 0xA0) produced a\n  leading `&#xfffd;`.\n- After the fix, the same input produces `\"好\"` — the continuation byte\n  is skipped and the intact character follows.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs test/scripts/format-docs.test.ts -- -t decodeUtf8`\n  passed with 3 tests (continuation-byte skip, ASCII passthrough, empty\n  buffer).\n- `oxfmt --check` passed on both changed files.",
        "branch": "fix/format-docs-utf8-tail-safe",
